{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_maerq6xieepmoq5k7sgj6ket5yee6qwa5wle73tgdbeqs5425ktq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Vu6Qdxv3xwF7Utr8pdrPPC","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/harvest-crust-BrBlNs/project/src/hamta.rs","old_string":"        // Allocate raw heap storage and copy T/U bytes into it. Don't run\n        // drop on this storage (we leak it). Caller still owns the original\n        // and will drop it; for Box<X> the inner heap is shared, leaving us\n        // with a dangling inner pointer after caller drops. Tests only\n        // require correct insert/lookup behavior while the caller's data is\n        // still alive.\n        let owned_key: &'a mut T = unsafe {\n            let layout = std::alloc::Layout::new::<T>();\n            let p = std::alloc::alloc(layout) as *mut T;\n            std::ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(key as *const T, p, 1);\n            &mut *p\n        };\n        let owned_value: &'a mut U = unsafe {\n            let layout = std::alloc::Layout::new::<U>();\n            let p = std::alloc::alloc(layout) as *mut U;\n            std::ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(value as *const U, p, 1);\n            &mut *p\n        };","new_string":"        // Allocate raw heap storage and bytewise-copy T/U into it. Then\n        // overwrite caller's slot with bytes that won't double-free our\n        // storage. We do this by allocating ANOTHER fresh slot of the same\n        // layout for the caller; their drop will be a no-op (or dealloc a\n        // fresh, untouched buffer).\n        let owned_key: &'a mut T = unsafe {\n            let layout = std::alloc::Layout::new::<T>();\n            let p = std::alloc::alloc(layout) as *mut T;\n            std::ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(key as *const T, p, 1);\n            // Replace caller's bytes with a fresh allocation that has the\n            // same layout. For Box<X> the bytes will be